            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: I have another question about your repo man example. You say we need that last sentence to capture him in a(6). But why wouldn't he be captured by the first sentence in a(6) too? Why isn't a repo man a classic debt collector under any definition, even the broad, the very broad ones you proffer for a(6), first sentence?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5cce377b82d7-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kavanaugh, jUSTICE KAVANAUGH: You are arguing, I think, that even if I disagree with you, we disagree with you on the first sentence, you win because of the third sentence, right?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5cce377b82d7-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 65,
              "start": 65
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Can I ask you one question on what you mean? Imagine we have a person just like this one, he's trying to enforce a securities interest and he doesn't ask for any deficiency payment."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5cce377b82d7-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 67,
              "start": 67
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: No, in other words, you're saying if the state were exactly the same, but it just didn't say anything about newspapers, then his client would win?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
            "evidence_ids": [
