              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Daniel L. Geyser, non\u2011judicial foreclosures are covered under the FDCPA as a direct attempt to collect a consumer\u2019s debt."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Daniel L. Geyser",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5cce377b82d7ce533311e22dbb0e548d9fbb8798219df7d38f23744f91fb7549",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5cce377b82d7-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Daniel L. Geyser, non\u2011judicial foreclosures are covered under the FDCPA as an indirect attempt because the foreclosure process is designed by law to automatically sell the consumer\u2019s house to obtain payment on the debt."
        }
      ],
